# Emotes and spells attached to lines, applied by tools/convert_play.py.
#
#   ROLE | first words of the line | action
#
# The action is an emote slash command (/laugh), a spell name (cast if the
# player knows it), or both: "Feign Death /lie" casts Feign Death if known,
# otherwise does /lie. Add "@Role" to direct it at whoever plays that role:
# "/kiss @Beatrice". Lines are matched ignoring punctuation and case.
#
# Stage directions like [Kisses her.] and [Hero swoons.] get an emote
# automatically. They can be matched here by their direction text (e.g. to
# give them a target), since they have no words.

BEATRICE  | I wonder that you will still be talking | /sigh @Benedick
BENEDICK  | What, my dear Lady Disdain               | /bow @Beatrice
BENEDICK  | Kisses her                               | /kiss @Beatrice
